          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>The more obstacles between you and your target, the deadlier your shots become, as you ricochet off multiple surfaces to hit them. When using @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Ricochet Shot], your shot can bounce off of any surface within your weapon's first three range increments and the target can't benefit from cover unless they have total cover on all sides.</p>\n<p>In addition, a creature must attempt a @Check[will|against:gunslinger] save against your class DC the first time in an encounter you attack it with a Ricochet Shot. If it fails, it's @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stunned]{Stunned 2} and is unable to determine where your shot originated.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 20
          },
